window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"u": "index.html", "t": "Descote V2", "h": "Critical technology, Human chemistry", "d": "Valves for hazardous fluids: chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear. Pre-engineered or tailor-made, designed and built in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Critical technology, Human chemistry Fit for challenge We handle Hazardous Fluids for Critical, Severe, applications. Our mission is to tackle the most challenging fluids and process conditions, while driving Engineering towards optimized performance and sustainability. “When Quality shall exceed the Standards…” Discover Chlorine related Chlorine, A-HCl and phosgene: PVC, polyurethane, polycarbonates and more. → Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (A-HF): refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, the nuclear fuel cycle. → Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN): methyl methacrylate (MMA), ABS and more. → Hydrogen related High temperature and high pressure hydrogen: valves defined project by project, up to Class 2500. → Other critical applications Bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. → All fluids & applications The fluid families we handle, on one page. → Safety Reliability Sustainability Industries chemicals chemicals agrochemicals agrochemicals petrochemicals petrochemicals nuclear nuclear All industries Fit for purpose We offer customisable & tailor-made Solutions Technology designed for professionals who understand and value the need for experience, precision, and authentic craftsmanship. Pre-engineered or tailored to meet your specific needs, we assist you to define the best technical solution. “What deserves to be done, deserves to be done well.” Nicolas Poussin Pre-engineered solutions Process / piping, instrumentation, storage, transport and fluid transfer: field-proven designs, adapted to your fluid. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Transport Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Engineering approach Built for one process Tailor-made in practice Engineering Development Reliability study Authentic Driven Flexible Human Chemistry At descote, we work with purpose: every valve and piece of equipment we deliver is built for a specific application and protects the people and installations that depend on it. “What is essential is invisible to the eye.” Antoine de Saint-Exupéry Discover Made in Feyzin, France From design to testing, the entire cycle is managed in-house. Watch our film Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will point you to the right solution. Send an inquiry Global Solution for you, International presence Where to find us ? From its earliest days, descote has looked beyond borders. Present in more than 70 countries, our teams collaborate worldwide to serve our customers where they are. Our network"}, {"u": "after-sales.html", "t": "After sales, spare parts & repair shops | Descote V2", "h": "Repairs and genuine parts for your descote valves", "d": "Genuine descote spare parts, repair shops close to your plants and local service to keep your valves fit for hazardous duty.", "x": "Home ▸ descote ▸ After sales Repairs and genuine parts for your descote valves A descote valve is built for long service in hazardous duty. When it needs care, genuine parts and repair shops close to your plants keep it that way. Repair shops close to your plants Our map lists repair shops close to your plants: select “Repair shops” to find the nearest one. Genuine descote spare parts Every descote valve has a unique serial number. Quote your valve's serial number: we identify the genuine parts that match it. Before you send a valve back Valves returned from hazardous service must be decontaminated first: contact us for the return procedure. Also at your service Expertise and repair Diagnosis and repair by our team in Feyzin. Instructions Installation, operation and maintenance instructions for each model. → Local stock Stock in Baton Rouge (USA); stock and after-sales service in Shanghai (China). → Your valve was defined for one service; its serial number lets us repair it to that same definition. Looking for a descote repair shop? Find the repair shops near your plant on our map, or send us an after-sales request. See the map After-sales request What next? Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. Resources FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Transport Instrumentation Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "case-studies.html", "t": "Case studies: valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Case studies", "d": "Anonymised field results: descote valves in chlorine, HF, HCN, nuclear and other severe services. Filter by industry, valve type and area.", "x": "Home ▸ Resources ▸ Case studies Case studies Anonymised results from chlorine, hydrogen fluoride (HF), hydrogen cyanide (HCN), nuclear and other severe duties. Success stories Customer names withheld. Industry All Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Fluid & application All Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Other critical applications Type of valve All Manual On-off Control 3-way Check Area All North America Europe Asia Reset Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Motorized valve mounted directly beneath a large storage vessel. Asia · Liquid chlorine Liquid chlorine storage tanks 1½\" and 2\" bellows sealed globe valves on liquid chlorine storage tanks, at −4 °C and about 15 bar: no problem in four years. Storage Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals Grey-painted piping and actuated valves on a skid in a process hall. Europe · Hydrogen fluoride (HF), gas mixtures Nuclear fuel: HF service since 1986 About 250 valves, including 3-way valves cycling every 12 minutes; no incident or HF leak reported by 2002. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Nuclear Actuated instrumentation valve among the stainless tubing of a laboratory installation. Europe · Heavy water, gases 950 valves for a nuclear research facility Manual, on-off, control and check valves up to 4\", fully documented in 1995; rated outstanding 20 years on. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Nuclear Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals Jacketed globe valve on its shipping crate: the outer jacket carries the heating medium. Asia · Molten salt 69 jacketed valves for molten salt 2500J bellows sealed valves with heat-jacketed body and bonnet keep molten salt at +400 °C. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals No case study matches these filters. Each valve was specified for its own fluid, conditions and plant. The same checks now apply to every duty: each bellows helium-tested, each valve pressure-tested and serial-numbered. Discuss your requirements Facing a similar duty? Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. Solutions All solutions Process / Piping Transport Storage Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Other critical applications Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "company.html", "t": "About us: valves for hazardous fluids since 1974 | Descote V2", "h": "Valve specialists for hazardous fluids since 1974", "d": "descote designs, manufactures and tests valves for hazardous fluids in Feyzin, France. Our history, values, key figures and international presence.", "x": "Home ▸ descote ▸ Company Valve specialists for hazardous fluids since 1974 descote designs, manufactures and tests valves for hazardous fluids, from toxic and corrosive chemicals to liquefied gases, in Feyzin, France. About descote Today descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries worldwide. Our core technology is the bellows sealed globe valve: a metal bellows seals the moving stem, with a packing as back-up. We also make gland packed valves, check valves, storage, transport and instrumentation valves, and fluid transfer ejectors. Our engineers work from your fluid, your process conditions and your specification, and the valve design follows from them. descote, the film Our people, our workshops and our test benches in Feyzin, in two and a half minutes. Inside our Feyzin factory From the bar of metal to the tested valve, everything is done under one roof. Our site in Feyzin, near Lyon Turning CNC machining Welding Assembly Testing Dimensional inspection Stores Finished valves, ready to ship Feyzin factory tour History 1974 Under new ownership, descote specialises in globe valves for hazardous fluids. 1979 The US Department of Energy accepts our valves for uranium hexafluoride (UF6) cylinders. 1983 First approval of our globe valves for liquid chlorine, by the BITC (Bureau International Technique du Chlore), which became Euro Chlor in 1989. 1989 ISO 9001 approval of our quality system; our valves are approved by Japan's High Pressure Gas Safety Institute (KHK). 1991 Our tank car valves are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). 1992 Our valves conform to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. 2009 descote leaves the Tyco group after ten years: the owner since 1974, his son and an American partner buy the company back. 2010 Renamed KD Valves under Tyco, the company becomes descote s.a.s. again. 2014 Our main globe valve series are certified SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) by exida, to IEC 61508. 2020 descote Inc. opens in Baton Rouge, USA. 2021 Euro Chlor approval (GEST 17/492) of models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC; fugitive emission qualification (leaks to the air) to EN ISO 15848-1 for selected models. 2025 Our service centre for Asia-Pacific opens in Shanghai. Values and commitments Purpose Every valve we deliver is built for a specific application and protects the people and installations that depend on it. Excellence We hold ourselves to the highest standards in engineering, manufacturing and service. Authenticity We stand authentic and faithful to our principles. Trust in people We promote team spirit and believe that diversity is a blessing. Key figures 50+ years designing valves for hazardous fluids 1 factory in Feyzin: design, manufacturing and testing under one roof 70+ countries where descote is present Certifications & approvals Every valve undergoes radiography, ultrasonic, magnetic particle and liquid penetrant testing of welds and machined parts, plus wall thickness, dimensional, surface finish and hardness checks. For the most critical applications, we add positive material identification (PMI), helium leak and fugitive emission testing. Each valve has a unique identification number and a Manufacturer Data Report, under our ISO 9001:2015 quality system, first approved in 1989. See our certificates → International presence Feyzin, France Headquarters, engineering and manufacturing. Baton Rouge, USA descote Inc.: local stock of valves and actuators. Shanghai, China descote Valve (Shanghai) Co., Ltd.: stock, customisation and after-sales for Asia-Pacific. Worldwide Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. → Critical Technology, Human Chemistry: our engineers define each valve with you, then our workshop builds, tests and traces it in Feyzin. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your fluid and conditions: our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solutions Tailor-made All solutions Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "cookies.html", "t": "Cookie Policy | Descote V2", "h": "Cookie Policy", "d": "Which cookies the descote website uses, what they do, how long they last and how to change your choice at any time.", "x": "Home ▸ Cookie Policy Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. What is a cookie? A cookie is a small text file stored on your device when you visit a website. It lets the site recognise your device and remember information about your visit. Cookies we use We measure audience with Matomo, hosted on our own website. _pk_id.* Audience measurement: stores a unique visit identifier. Lifetime: 13 months. _pk_ref.* Audience measurement: records how you arrived on the site. Lifetime: 6 months. _pk_ses.* Audience measurement: stores your visit data temporarily. Lifetime: 30 minutes. hasConsent Remembers your cookie choice so the banner is not shown again. Lifetime: 7 months. External services Some features rely on external providers, which may set their own cookies or collect technical data such as your IP address. Form protection Anti-spam check on our forms (currently Google reCAPTCHA). Your choices You can accept or refuse non-essential cookies in the cookie banner. To change your choice, delete this site's cookies in your browser: the banner will appear again. You can also block cookies in your browser settings; some features may then no longer work. How long we keep data Cookies and browsing data are kept for 13 months at most. To find out how we handle personal data, please read our Privacy Policy. A question about cookies? Write to info@descote.com. Privacy Policy How descote handles your personal data. What next? Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Legal notices Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website."}, {"u": "descote.html", "t": "About descote: company, presence, service, careers | Descote V2", "h": "Critical Technology, Human Chemistry", "d": "Who descote is, where to find its representatives and repair shops, how it services its valves and how to join its teams in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Home ▸ descote Critical Technology, Human Chemistry Who we are, where to find us, how we look after your valves and how to join our teams: everything about descote, from our factory in Feyzin, France. About us Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France. Discover → Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Discover → After sales Genuine spare parts, repair in Feyzin and repair shops close to your plants. Discover → Join us Join our teams in Feyzin, near Lyon, France. Discover → descote, the film Our people, our workshops and our test benches in Feyzin, in two and a half minutes. Watch the film → Every descote valve is engineered for its fluid and its process, then built, tested and traced in our factory in Feyzin. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your fluid and your process. Our engineers will get back to you. Send an inquiry What next? Overview Solutions Pre-engineered and tailor-made valves for process piping, instrumentation, storage and transport, plus jet ejectors for fluid transfer. Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. Overview Industries Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals and nuclear."}, {"u": "faq.html", "t": "FAQ: bellows sealed valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Frequently asked questions", "d": "Answers on descote bellows sealed globe valves: technology, selection, Euro Chlor, SIL, fugitive emissions, testing, spare parts and repairs.", "x": "Home ▸ Resources ▸ FAQ Frequently asked questions What engineers and buyers ask us most. All Technology Selection Certifications Quality Service Why a bellows sealed globe valve for hazardous fluids? The stem, the usual leak path, is sealed by a welded multi-ply metal bellows, backed up by a packing. 2100 or 2500 series: what is the difference? In the 2100, the bellows is protected from the flow, inside the bonnet. In the 2500, the bellows is in the flow, which suits fluids that polymerise or crystallise. Can a globe valve replace a gate, plug or ball valve? It can, at the same face-to-face (installed length). Globe valves pass less flow than full-bore valves, so we check your flow coefficient (Cv) first. Which fluids do you handle? Mainly hazardous fluids where a small leak can cause serious harm (ASME B31.3 Category M), such as chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl), phosgene, hydrogen fluoride (HF) and hydrogen cyanide (HCN); also bromine, hydrogen, ethylene oxide, molten salts and ammonia. For any other fluid, send us its safety data sheet. What do you need to prepare a quotation? Fluid, water content, design pressure and temperatures, size, class, end connections, actuation, applicable standards and country of installation. Can you build to our own specification? Yes, including your country's codes; any deviation is agreed before manufacture. Earlier on, we can help with sizing and material selection. Do your chlorine valves meet Euro Chlor recommendations? Models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC are Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492), within defined sizes and classes. Approval certificates on request. Are your valves rated for safety integrity level (SIL)? Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 2200/2300 and actuators are SIL 3 capable (IEC 61508:2010), certified by exida. The SIL of your safety function is calculated on the whole loop. Do your valves meet fugitive emission standards? Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500 are type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and German TA Luft rules, within stated limits. Do you supply valves for HF alkylation units? Yes. Our bellows sealed globe valves are approved by UOP (a Honeywell company) for HF alkylation service. How is each valve tested? Every valve undergoes radiography, ultrasonic, magnetic particle and liquid penetrant testing of welds and machined parts, wall thickness, dimensional, surface finish and hardness checks, then shell and seat tests. For the most critical applications, we also offer positive material identification (PMI) and helium leak and fugitive emission testing. What documents come with each valve? A Manufacturer Data Report tied to the valve's unique serial number, with EN 10204 3.1 material certificates and test results. How do I order spare parts? Quote your valve's serial number: we identify the genuine parts that match it. Can I return a valve for repair? Yes. Valves returned from hazardous service must be decontaminated first: contact us for the return procedure. A repair shop close to your plant may also help. Most answers depend on your duty: we define each valve around it, then test it before shipment. Still have a question? Our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. descote After sales Genuine spare parts, repair in Feyzin and repair shops close to your plants. Solutions Process / Piping All solutions Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Other critical applications"}, {"u": "fluid-chlorine.html", "t": "Valves for chlorine, HCl and phosgene | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for chlorine chemistry", "d": "Bellows sealed globe valves for chlorine, anhydrous HCl and phosgene. Chlorine valves Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492).", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Chlorine related Valves for chlorine chemistry Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene are toxic, corrosive and react with moisture. From electrolysis to tank car loading, descote valves keep them contained. Application families Examples of processes in the chemical and agrochemical industries where our valves handle chlorine, hydrogen chloride and phosgene: Chloromethanes Solvents and chemical intermediates. Chemicals PVC From vinyl chloride (VCM) to PVC resin. Chemicals Polyurethane Isocyanates (MDI, TDI, HDI), made with phosgene. Chemicals Polycarbonates Made with phosgene. Chemicals Epichlorohydrin A chlorinated intermediate for epoxy resins. Chemicals TiO2 Titanium dioxide pigment. Chemicals Polysilicon and rare earths Base materials of the semiconductor and electronics industries. Chemicals Synthetic rubbers Chlorine-based elastomers. Chemicals Pesticides and insecticides Crop protection products. Agrochemicals What chlorine demands Liquid chlorine and dry chlorine gas Moisture makes chlorine corrosive: every valve is degreased and dried for halogen service. Anhydrous HCl It cools sharply as it expands, so materials are chosen for the lowest temperature. Phosgene Extremely toxic. Double-containment designs are available on request. Solutions for this fluid Pre-engineered solutions Bellows sealed globe valves 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC, instrumentation valves 2020, Dual Tek tank valves 2200 and 2300, and tank car valves 921, 922 and 925. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Transport Pre-engineered solutions → Tailor-made engineering When no standard design fits your chlorine process: a valve developed with you, from calculations to qualification. How we engineer it → Each chlorine valve is defined for its line and standard, then traced from raw material to final test. Certifications & approvals Approvals and certifications vary with the fluid. Certificates on request. Euro Chlor GEST 17/492 Models 2100B (2100BE for angle valves), 2100BAT and 2100BAC, 1\" to 6\" (DN25 to DN150): PN40 / Class 300 for liquid chlorine and dry gaseous chlorine; PN16, PN25 / Class 150 for dry gaseous chlorine. First Euro Chlor approval in 1983. Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6 Our full range of valves for chlorine service, liquid or gas, conforms to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. descote has been a member of the Chlorine Institute since 1985. Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). Transport approvals Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) for railcar transport are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Our ISO container valves are ISO 10297 certified and comply with RID/ADR. SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010. KHK (Japan) Our valves are approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request On-off actuated bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAT Request Control bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAC Request All literature → FAQ Why a bellows sealed globe valve for dry chlorine? The disc lifts straight off the seat without sliding friction, so deposits do not jam it; a welded metal bellows seals the stem. Do you supply valves for wet chlorine? Wet chlorine needs different materials: send us your conditions for review. All questions → Other fluids & applications Fluorine related Cyanide related Other critical applications Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Discuss your requirements Share your fluid, operating conditions and standards: we will define the valve for your line. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solution Storage The Dual Tek system: a bellows sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve, at the top or bottom of large tanks. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "fluid-cn.html", "t": "Valves for hydrogen cyanide (HCN) service | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for hydrogen cyanide chemistry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for hydrogen cyanide (HCN) service: methyl methacrylate (MMA) and acrylic glass, amino acids, acrylic rubber.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Cyanide related Valves for hydrogen cyanide chemistry Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) is a building block for methyl methacrylate (MMA), acrylic glass and amino acids. It is extremely toxic, flammable and can polymerise inside the line. Application families Examples of processes in the chemical industry where our valves handle hydrogen cyanide: MMA and acrylic glass Methyl methacrylate (MMA) and its polymer, acrylic glass (PMMA). Chemicals ABS Acrylonitrile butadiene styrene plastics. Chemicals Amino acids Synthesis of amino acids. Chemicals Acrylic rubber Specialty synthetic rubber. Chemicals What HCN demands Polymerisation Stagnant HCN can polymerise in packings and cavities and seize the stem. In our 2500 series, the bellows sits in the flow, which keeps it flushed. Toxicity A welded metal bellows, backed by a secondary packing, contains the fluid at the stem. Solidification Products that solidify as they cool need heated, jacketed valves. Solutions for this fluid Pre-engineered solutions Bellows sealed globe valves 2500, 2500BAT and 1500B with the bellows in the flow, instrumentation valves 2020, and isolation valves for HCN storage tanks. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Pre-engineered solutions → Tailor-made engineering Heated jacketed valves, and any other valve your HCN process requires, developed with you. How we engineer it → For HCN, the design follows the process: bellows position, heating and materials are chosen service by service. Certifications & approvals Approvals and certifications vary with the fluid. Certificates on request. Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010. PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Request All literature → FAQ Model 2500 or 2100 for HCN? It depends on the process. Our 2500, with its bellows in the flow, is recommended where polymerisation is a risk; our engineers confirm the choice for each service. Can valves be heated? Yes. Jacketed versions keep body and bonnet at process temperature. All questions → Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Other critical applications Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid, its stabilisation, temperature and pressure. We will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia."}, {"u": "fluid-fluorine.html", "t": "Valves for HF alkylation and fluorine chemistry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for fluorine chemistry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for anhydrous HF and fluorine chemistry: refrigerants, HF alkylation, BF3, semiconductors and the nuclear fuel cycle.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Fluorine related Valves for fluorine chemistry Anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (A-HF) is the backbone of fluorine chemistry, from refrigerants to HF alkylation. Application families Examples of processes in the chemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries where our valves handle hydrogen fluoride and fluorinated gases: Refrigerants CFC, HCFC, HFC and HFO refrigerants. Chemicals Fluorine and HF industry Hydrogen fluoride and fluorinated gases such as NF3, BF3 and ClF3. Chemicals Semiconductors Fluorinated electronic gases used to make chips and displays. Chemicals HF alkylation / LAB Refinery alkylation units and linear alkylbenzene (LAB), with hydrogen fluoride as catalyst. Petrochemicals Nuclear fuel cycle Uranium hexafluoride (UF6): conversion and enrichment. Nuclear → What HF demands Toxicity Highly toxic: a welded metal bellows, backed by packing, seals the stem, the usual leak path. Deep burns HF causes deep burns on contact: every joint and seal counts. Low boiling point Anhydrous HF boils at 19.5 °C: helium leak testing is available for the most critical applications. HF alkylation Our valves for HF alkylation units, their approvals and field references are presented on our Petrochemicals page. Petrochemicals → Nuclear: fluorine at the heart of the fuel cycle Uranium conversion and enrichment rely on hydrogen fluoride, fluorine and uranium hexafluoride (UF6). See our nuclear page. Nuclear → Solutions for this fluid Pre-engineered solutions 2100HF series bellows sealed globe and gate valves, 8000 lift check valves, instrumentation valves 2020, Dual Tek tank valves 2200 and 2300 for A-HF, and 925/926 tank car valves. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Transport Pre-engineered solutions → Tailor-made engineering When no standard design fits your HF process: a valve developed with you, from calculations to qualification. How we engineer it → In HF service, trims, actuators and extensions are engineered for each unit, not picked from a catalogue. Certifications & approvals Approvals and certifications vary with the fluid. Certificates on request. HF alkylation (UOP) Our bellows sealed globe and gate valves are UOP approved for use on HF alkylation. Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). Transport approvals Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) for railcar transport are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Our ISO container valves are ISO 10297 certified and comply with RID/ADR. SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010. Nuclear (UF6) ASME NQA-1, 10 CFR 50, 10 CFR 71 and 10 CFR 21; UF6 cylinder valves to ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195; approved by the US Department of Energy. PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature HF alkylation: process valves Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Request All literature → FAQ Do you handle fluorine gas (F2)? Fluorine is the strongest known oxidiser: we review each request case by case. All questions → Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Other critical applications Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, its water content and your operating conditions. We will propose the right valve. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities."}, {"u": "fluid-other.html", "t": "Valves for other critical applications | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for other critical applications", "d": "Valves for hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services, defined for each fluid.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications ▸ Other critical applications Valves for other critical applications Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry are our core business, but the same engineering serves other severe duties: high-pressure hydrogen, toxic gases, very high temperatures. Application families Hydrogen High temperature and high pressure: valves up to Class 2500, defined project by project. Bromine Bromine and its compounds, toxic and highly corrosive. Ethylene oxide Toxic and flammable, and liable to polymerise. Molten salts Heated jacketed valves stop the salt from freezing in the line. Ammonia Toxic liquefied gas: our 2200/2300 tank valves are designed for it. What severe services demand Temperature From very low to very high temperatures: body, bellows and seat materials are selected for each service. Pressure Dedicated high-pressure series, bellows sealed or gland packed. Functional safety We supply the certification data of our valves and actuators; the safety integrity level (SIL) achieved depends on the complete loop. Solutions for this fluid Pre-engineered solutions Manual, on-off and control valves (2100BAT, 2500 series), instrumentation valves 2020, and Dual Tek tank valves 2200 and 2300 for liquefied gases such as ammonia. Process / Piping Instrumentation Storage Pre-engineered solutions → Tailor-made engineering Heated jacketed valves, special materials and tests: any valve your process requires, developed with you. How we engineer it → Outside our core fields, the method stays the same: the valve is defined from your fluid data, then shell- and seat-tested before delivery. Certifications & approvals Approvals and certifications vary with the fluid. Certificates on request. Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010. KHK (Japan) Our valves are approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals Jacketed globe valve on its shipping crate: the outer jacket carries the heating medium. Asia · Molten salt 69 jacketed valves for molten salt 2500J bellows sealed valves with heat-jacketed body and bonnet keep molten salt at +400 °C. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Request BIMATIC linear pneumatic actuator Request All literature → FAQ Is my fluid within your scope? If it is toxic, corrosive, flammable, very hot or under high pressure, it may well be. Send us its safety data sheet and your operating conditions. All questions → Other fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Discuss your requirements A severe service outside our usual fields? Describe it: our engineers will tell you what we can do. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Industry Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units."}, {"u": "fluids.html", "t": "Fluids & applications: valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Hazardous fluids we handle", "d": "Chlorine, fluorine, hydrogen cyanide, hydrogen and other critical fluids: descote valves are defined for each fluid, process and standard.", "x": "Home ▸ Fluids & applications Hazardous fluids we handle descote works where a leak is not an option. Choose your fluid to see its main applications, what it demands and our solutions for it. Our fluid families Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Discover → Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases: refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, the nuclear fuel cycle. Discover → Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN): methyl methacrylate (MMA) and acrylic glass, amino acids, acrylic rubber. Discover → Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Discover → What makes a fluid critical? Toxic, corrosive, flammable or pyrophoric: many of the fluids we handle are Category M fluid services under ASME B31.3, where one small leak can cause serious harm. One method, whatever the fluid The fluids change; the method does not. Our engineers define each valve for its fluid, its operating conditions and your site standards. It is then made in Feyzin, France, tested and fully traceable. Prefer to start from your sector? Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals or nuclear: start from your sector to find the fluids and solutions that concern it. Industries → Same method for every fluid: the valve is engineered for the service, never the other way round. Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will point you to the right solution. Send an inquiry What next? Overview Industries Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals and nuclear. Overview Solutions Pre-engineered and tailor-made valves for process piping, instrumentation, storage and transport, plus jet ejectors for fluid transfer. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up."}, {"u": "industries.html", "t": "Industries we serve | Descote V2", "h": "Industries we serve", "d": "descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries. Choose your sector, or start from your fluid.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries Industries we serve descote serves the chemical, agrochemical, petrochemical and nuclear industries worldwide. Choose your sector to see the applications we serve and the solutions that fit. Our sectors Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Discover → Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Discover → Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Discover → Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Discover → Prefer to start from your fluid? Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids: start from your fluid in Fluids & applications. Both lead to the same product families. Fluids & applications → Whatever your sector, each valve is defined for its fluid, then tested and traced. Discuss your requirements Tell us your industry, fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will point you to the right solution. Send an inquiry What next? Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. Overview Solutions Pre-engineered and tailor-made valves for process piping, instrumentation, storage and transport, plus jet ejectors for fluid transfer. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up."}, {"u": "industry-agrochemicals.html", "t": "Valves for the agrochemical industry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for the agrochemical industry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for crop protection plants: herbicides, insecticides, fungicides. Chlorine chemistry and other toxic fluids kept contained.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Agrochemicals Valves for the agrochemical industry Making crop protection products can involve hazardous fluids such as chlorine and its derivatives. descote valves keep them contained. descote in agrochemicals We serve producers of crop protection products, or pesticides. Their plants can handle the same hazardous fluids as the chemical industry, such as chlorine, phosgene, anhydrous HF or hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Applications we serve Herbicides Crop protection against weeds. Insecticides Crop protection against insects. Fungicides Crop protection against fungal diseases. Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual, on-off and control, for toxic and corrosive process fluids. Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves for liquefied toxic gases such as chlorine, with remote closure. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for gauges, transmitters and sampling points. Explore the range → Transport Tank car valves, and Dual Tek valves for ISO tank containers, for chlorine and other liquefied toxic gases. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Valves defined from your fluid data when no existing design fits. How we engineer it → Whatever the active ingredient, your valve starts from your fluid data. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. ISO 9001 Quality management system approved since 1989. PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025, 2200/2300 and actuators are SIL 3 capable (IEC 61508:2010). Chlorine Models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC are approved for liquid chlorine (Euro Chlor GEST 17/492). Our valves conform to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. KHK (Japan) Our valves are approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). Transport approvals Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Our ISO container valves are ISO 10297 certified and comply with RID/ADR. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Agrochemical case studies are in preparation. Tell us about your application. Share your application All case studies → Related literature Chemical programme: descote in the chemical industry Request All literature → Other industries Chemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Tell us your fluid and operating conditions. Our engineers will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more."}, {"u": "industry-chemicals.html", "t": "Valves for the chemical industry | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for the chemical industry", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry: PVC, isocyanates, refrigerants, acrylics. Made in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Chemicals Valves for the chemical industry Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry are our core business. descote valves keep their toxic and corrosive fluids contained. descote in chemicals In chemical plants, our valves handle chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl), phosgene, hydrogen fluoride (HF) and hydrogen cyanide (HCN), from storage tanks and tank cars to process lines. Each valve is defined for its fluid and its line. Applications we serve PVC Chlorine and hydrogen chloride lines, from vinyl chloride to PVC. Isocyanates Chlorine and phosgene service for the building blocks of polyurethanes. Other chlorine chemistry Chloromethanes, polysilicon, synthetic rubbers. Fluorochemicals Refrigerants, built on anhydrous hydrogen fluoride. Acrylics Methyl methacrylate (MMA) and acrylic glass, on the hydrogen cyanide route. Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual, on-off and control, with Euro Chlor approved models for chlorine. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for gauges, transmitters and sampling points. Explore the range → Storage Top and bottom tank valves for liquefied toxic gases, with remote closure. Explore the range → Transport Tank car valves, and Dual Tek valves for ISO tank containers. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Valves defined with you when no existing design fits, such as heated jacketed valves. How we engineer it → Every valve is made in Feyzin, France, then tested and fully traceable. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. ISO 9001 Quality management system approved since 1989. PED and ATEX Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and ATEX directive 2014/34/EU (explosive atmospheres). Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025, 2200/2300 and actuators are SIL 3 capable (IEC 61508:2010). Chlorine Models 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC are approved for liquid chlorine (Euro Chlor GEST 17/492). Our valves conform to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. KHK (Japan) Our valves are approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). Transport approvals Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Our ISO container valves are ISO 10297 certified and comply with RID/ADR. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals Valves around a process vessel, on a circular access platform. Europe · Fluorinated fluids (refrigerants) Refrigerants: in service since 1993 On corrosive, toxic fluorinated fluids, some valves ran without maintenance from 1993 to at least 2016. Process / Piping Fluorine related Chemicals Bellows sealed globe valve next to a sampling station. North America · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) One valve, 14 shutdowns avoided An automated 2502 angle valve (1997) replaced a draw-off valve that failed at least twice a year; no failure by 2010. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Chemical programme: descote in the chemical industry Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request All literature → Other industries Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Tell us your product, your fluid and your operating conditions. Our engineers will define the valve with you. Send an inquiry What next? Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "industry-nuclear.html", "t": "Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle | Descote V2", "h": "Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle", "d": "Bellows sealed valves and steam jet ejectors for UF6 conversion and enrichment, fuel fabrication, reactors, reprocessing and research facilities.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Nuclear Valves and ejectors for the nuclear fuel cycle Nuclear facilities handle fluids that are both chemically aggressive and radioactive. descote has served the nuclear industry since 1975. descote in the nuclear industry We supply valves and steam jet ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion and enrichment to fuel fabrication, reactors and reprocessing, and to research facilities. Where the fluid is radioactive, our ejectors move it with no moving parts. Our products: valves for UF6 cylinders 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G, process valves and steam jets. The entire cycle (calculations, design, research, prototyping, testing, qualification, industrial production), as well as nuclear project management, documentation and inspection, is covered by our Quality Assurance organization, certified to ISO 9001 and NQA-1. The nuclear fuel cycle From conversion to reprocessing, our valves and steam jets are used at almost every step of the cycle. descote equipment used at each step Across the fuel cycle Conversion Bellows sealed valves for anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (HF) and uranium hexafluoride (UF6) lines. Enrichment Valves for UF6 process lines. Fuel fabrication HF lines in the conversion of UF6 to uranium oxide. UF6 transport Model 1000, our 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G, to ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195; also 1-inch plugs and ¾-inch valves for sampling bottles. → Reactors High-pressure globe valves, gland packed or bellows sealed, for primary and secondary circuits and test reactors; steam jet ejectors for reactor safety. Reprocessing and MOX Steam jet ejectors with biological protection transfer highly corrosive and radioactive liquids in reprocessing and mixed-oxide (MOX) fuel plants. Research facilities Bellows sealed valves for heavy water (D2O), lead-lithium and other special fluids, and steam jet ejectors. What the fuel cycle demands Chemistry and radioactivity UF6 reacts with moisture to form HF. Tightness to the atmosphere comes first. Frequent cycling Some on-off valves operate very often: bellows life must be designed and proven. Nuclear qualification Seismic calculation, radiation resistance and nuclear validation tests where required; complete documentation and traceability for every valve. Fluids & applications Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves, manual and on-off, for the fluorine and chlorine chemistry of the UF6 cycle. 2100B 4025 Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for measuring and sampling points. Explore the range → Storage The Dual Tek system combines a bellows sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve, at the top or bottom of large tanks. Explore the range → Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Steam jet ejectors for radioactive fluids and reactor safety, characterised on our own test bench in Feyzin. Explore the range → Transport UF6 cylinder valves and plugs, tank car valves and Dual Tek valves for ISO containers. UF6 valve – Model 1000 Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Valves and ejectors defined with you when no existing design fits. How we engineer it → From high-cycling on-off valves to steam jet ejectors, each piece of equipment is engineered for its step of the fuel cycle. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. Nuclear quality assurance Quality assurance to ISO 9001, ASME NQA-1, 10 CFR 50 Appendix B, 10 CFR 71 and 10 CFR 21. ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195 Our 1-inch UF6 cylinder valves and plugs are designed to these standards. US Department of Energy descote is approved by the US Department of Energy (DOE) and has supplied UF6 cylinder valves since 1978. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Grey-painted piping and actuated valves on a skid in a process hall. Europe · Hydrogen fluoride (HF), gas mixtures Nuclear fuel: HF service since 1986 About 250 valves, including 3-way valves cycling every 12 minutes; no incident or HF leak reported by 2002. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Nuclear Actuated instrumentation valve among the stainless tubing of a laboratory installation. Europe · Heavy water, gases 950 valves for a nuclear research facility Manual, on-off, control and check valves up to 4\", fully documented in 1995; rated outstanding 20 years on. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Nuclear All case studies → Related literature Nuclear programme: descote in the nuclear industry Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request All literature → FAQ How do you handle nuclear quality requirements? Our quality assurance covers the entire cycle: calculations, design, prototyping, testing, qualification, production, documentation and inspection. Send your requirements with your inquiry: documentation and traceability are agreed with you for each project. All questions → Other industries Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Discuss your requirements Describe your step of the fuel cycle, your fluid and your quality requirements. Our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Steam jets for radioactive fluids: thermodynamic pumps without moving parts. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "industry-petrochemicals.html", "t": "Valves for refineries and HF alkylation | Descote V2", "h": "Valves for refineries and HF alkylation", "d": "Bellows sealed valves for refineries and HF alkylation units, approved by UOP (a Honeywell company) for HF alkylation service.", "x": "Home ▸ Industries ▸ Petrochemicals Valves for refineries and HF alkylation In refineries, descote valves contain anhydrous hydrogen fluoride (HF) in HF alkylation units, and serve other severe duties. HF alkylation Anhydrous HF is the catalyst that makes alkylate for cleaner fuels. Our bellows sealed globe valves are approved by UOP (a Honeywell company) for HF alkylation service. Applications we serve HF alkylation units Isolation and on-off valves for HF service. Refineries Other severe refinery services. Fluids & applications Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Solutions for this industry ← → Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe and gate valves, gland packed valves and lift check valves for HF service. 2100HF series 8000 lift check valve Explore the range → Storage Dual Tek top and bottom tank valves for anhydrous HF. Explore the range → Instrumentation Small-bore bellows sealed valves for HF service. Explore the range → Tailor-made engineering Trims, actuators and extensions engineered for each unit. How we engineer it → Every valve is examined and pressure-tested in Feyzin, France, with helium leak testing for the most critical applications. Proven in the field Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Globe valve fitted with position instrumentation on a process line. Europe · Hot oil Hot-oil emergency shutdown valve An 8-inch on-off bellows sealed valve, helium-tested for fugitive emissions, designed for safety integrity level 2 (SIL 2). Process / Piping Other critical applications Petrochemicals All case studies → Related literature HF alkylation: process valves Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Request All literature → FAQ Can a globe valve replace the plug valves of an HF alkylation unit? It can: versions with the same face-to-face dimensions fit existing piping. A globe valve has a lower flow coefficient (Cv), so we check the required flow with you first. All questions → Other industries Chemicals Agrochemicals Nuclear Discuss your requirements Send us your unit, fluid and piping class. We will propose the right valve and trim. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Fluid & application Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases: refrigerants, HF alkylation, semiconductors, the nuclear fuel cycle."}, {"u": "literature.html", "t": "Literature: brochures & manuals | Descote V2", "h": "Literature", "d": "Technical brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions for descote bellows sealed valves and actuators, available on request.", "x": "Home ▸ Resources ▸ Literature Literature Brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions for our valves and actuators, sent on request. Maintenance manuals and Operating and Safety Instructions Every descote valve has its maintenance manual (IOM) and its Operating and Safety Instructions, the short leaflet on storage, handling and installation. They are not published online: tick the documents you need below and leave your email, we send them to you. Every document here describes a starting point; your valve is then defined around your specification. Documents Type All Technical brochure Maintenance manual Safety instructions Category All Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage General Reset Chemical programme: descote in the chemical industry Technical brochure · General Request Gland packed globe valve, Model 1500B Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request On-off actuated bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAT Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Control bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100BAC Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request 3-way valves, Models 3100 & 3500 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Lift check valve, Model 8000 Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request BIMATIC linear pneumatic actuator Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request HF alkylation: process valves Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request HF alkylation: small-size valves Technical brochure · Process / Piping Request Instrumentation bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2020 Technical brochure · Instrumentation Request Storage tank valves, Models 2200 & 2300 Technical brochure · Storage Request Trailer & rail transportation valves Technical brochure · Transport Request 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders Technical brochure · Transport Request Nuclear programme: descote in the nuclear industry Technical brochure · General Request Models 1500B & 1500BAT Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2100B, 2100BAT & 3-way valves Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2500 & 2500BAT Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Models 2100HF, 2100HFAT & 2100HFAC Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Model 8000 lift check valve Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Model 2020 instrumentation valve Maintenance manual · Instrumentation Request Models 2200 & 2300 storage valves Maintenance manual · Storage Request Models 921, 925 & 926 tank car valves Maintenance manual · Transport Request BIMATIC actuator Maintenance manual · Process / Piping Request Operating & safety instructions, all models Safety instructions · General Request No document matches these filters. Your valve, your documents Brochures show our base designs. The valve you order is engineered for your duty and ships with its own test records and material certificates. Request documents Full name * Company * Business email * Country * Industry Select… Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Other Documents * We send each document in the language of your country. I agree to the Privacy Policy . * Send my request Mock-up: nothing is sent. * required Thank you — your request has been noted. The descote team will get back to you shortly. Didn't find what you were looking for? Send an inquiry What next? Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Resources FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solutions Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage All solutions Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "quality-certification.html", "t": "Certifications & approvals: quality, tests and approvals | Descote V2", "h": "Quality you can trace, certificates you can check", "d": "ISO 9001 quality management, in-house testing and full traceability. Browse descote certificates and approvals: free download or on request.", "x": "Home ▸ Resources ▸ Certifications & approvals Quality you can trace, certificates you can check Our certificates, approvals and declarations, and the quality system behind every valve, from raw material to shipment. Our approach to quality Our quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 by LRQA, with a first ISO approval in 1989. It covers design, manufacturing, sales and customer service for our valves and ejectors. For each application, we define the valve's design, materials, inspection and test plan, and final preparation. “When Quality shall exceed the Standards…” Checks built into production Non-destructive examination On every valve: radiography, ultrasonic, magnetic particle and liquid penetrant testing of welds and machined parts. Dimensional checks Wall thickness, dimensions, surface finish and hardness, checked on every valve. Pressure tests Hydrostatic body test and seat tightness test on every valve. For the most critical applications Additional in-house testing: positive material identification (PMI), helium leak and fugitive emission testing. Preparation Cleaning, drying, painting and tagging before shipment. Traceability A unique identification number links each valve to its Manufacturer Data Report and EN 10204 3.1 material certificates. Tailor-made down to the paperwork: each valve ships with a certificate that names your specification and records its own tests. Our certificates and approvals Documents marked “on request” are sent after a short form, in their current revision. All Location Technical Quality management ISO 9001:2015 Quality management system certified by LRQA; ISO 9001 approved since 1989. Free download EcoVadis Business sustainability rating: descote is assessed by EcoVadis. On request Request → AAR M-1003 Quality assurance for rail tank car valves (Association of American Railroads). On request Request → Nuclear quality assurance Quality assurance for nuclear projects to ASME NQA-1, 10 CFR 50 Appendix B, 10 CFR 71 and 10 CFR 21. On request Request → ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195 1-inch valves and plugs for UF6 cylinders 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G, designed to ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195. On request Request → US Department of Energy descote is approved by the US Department of Energy (DOE) and has supplied UF6 cylinder valves to the global industry since 1978. USA On request Request → Euro Chlor GEST 17/492 Models 2100B (2100BE for angle valves), 2100BAT and 2100BAC, 1\" to 6\" (DN25 to DN150): PN40 / Class 300 for liquid chlorine and dry gaseous chlorine; PN16, PN25 / Class 150 for dry gaseous chlorine. First Euro Chlor approval in 1983. Free download Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6 Our full range of valves for chlorine service, liquid or gas, conforms to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. descote has been a member of the Chlorine Institute since 1985. On request Request → SIL 3 capable (safety integrity level) Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010, certified by exida. Free download Fugitive emissions (leaks to the air) Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2200 & 2300, 2500, 3100 & 3500, 2100HF, 2100HFAT and 7300HF are certified to ISO 15848-1 (class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). On request Request → Hydrogen fluoride (HF) alkylation Our bellows sealed globe and gate valves are UOP approved for use on HF alkylation. On request Request → ISO 10297 and RID/ADR Valves for ISO tank containers certified to ISO 10297 and compliant with the RID (rail) and ADR (road) dangerous goods regulations. On request Request → Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU Module H (full quality assurance): globe and lift check valves. European Union On request Request → ATEX (explosive atmospheres) Globe valves for potentially explosive atmospheres, compliant with directive 2014/34/EU; technical file lodged with a notified body. European Union On request Request → AAR tank car valves Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). North America On request Request → Transport Canada TP14877 922 and 925 tank car valves, with their 926 internal check valve, compliant with standard TP14877. Canada On request Request → Canadian Registration Number (CRN) Registration of our valve range in Canada. Canada On request Request → China special equipment licence 2100 and 2500 manual and on-off valves. China On request Request → KHK (Japan) Approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). Japan On request Request → No document matches this filter. Need another document? Ask for a certificate, a declaration or a test report. Request a document What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. Resources Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Transport Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "resources.html", "t": "Resources: case studies, certifications, literature | Descote V2", "h": "Resources", "d": "Field results, technical literature, certificates and answers on descote bellows sealed valves for chlorine, HF, HCN and nuclear duties.", "x": "Home ▸ Resources Resources Case studies, certifications & approvals, literature and answers to common questions: the resources we make available. Explore our resources Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. Discover → Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Discover → Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions. Discover → FAQ Short answers to the questions engineers and buyers ask us most often. Discover → Every resource here comes back to one idea: a valve defined for its fluid, then tested and traced. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your application. We will send you the documents and references that match it. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. descote Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France. Solutions Process / Piping Storage Tailor-made Fluids & applications Chlorine related Fluorine related Cyanide related Other critical applications Industries Nuclear"}, {"u": "solution-fluid-transfer.html", "t": "Steam jet ejectors for fluid transfer | Descote V2", "h": "Fluid transfer & jet ejectors", "d": "Steam jet ejectors for radioactive and corrosive fluids: about 2,500 units at La Hague, also in Japan and the USA. Designed, qualified and made by descote.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Fluid transfer & jet ejectors In nuclear applications, fluid transfer is safely and efficiently achieved through the use of jets and ejectors. Safe and efficient fluid handling in nuclear applications In nuclear applications, fluid transfer is safely and efficiently achieved through the use of jets and ejectors. Utilizing steam, air or hydro power, these jet pumps fulfil several critical functions: Fluid transfer: reliable transport of radioactive, contaminated and corrosive fluids. Process control: creating vacuum environments, managing syphons and driving evaporation. Fluid dynamics: facilitating continuous mixing and agitation of fluids. Steam ejectors for radioactive fluids: proven technology on an international scale Specialized equipment for La Hague For the La Hague facility in France, descote developed specialized safety equipment to handle highly contaminated fluids. These steam jets work as thermodynamic pumps with no moving parts. They are designed to transfer highly corrosive and radioactive fluids, and feature: Biological protection, configured as fixed or EMEM-removable units. EAS ejectors for reactor safety. Our steam jet designs Immerged Monobloc Dismountable, with biological protection From R&D to industrial production Developed under an R&D contract with SGN/ORANO, this equipment required expertise across the entire development process, including engineering, seismic calculations, radiation resistance, nuclear validation testing and industrial production. Proven technology deployed worldwide Around 2,500 units have been delivered to La Hague. This proven technology has also been supplied to Japan for the Rokkasho Mura reprocessing plant and to the United States for the Shaw/Areva MOX project. End-to-end nuclear engineering expertise descote provides recognized expertise built on extensive experience in the nuclear industry. Our teams can meet a wide range of specifications and manage the development of new products. The entire cycle (calculations, design, research, prototyping, testing, qualification and industrial production) is covered by our Quality Assurance organization, along with nuclear project management, documentation and inspection. Our organization is certified to ISO 9001 and NQA-1. Calculation Fluid transfer More than 600 profiles tested Pre-engineered or tailor-made Start from a proven ejector design, or develop a new one with us, from calculations to qualification tests. Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Radioactive and toxic fluids No rotating part and no seal to wear: very little maintenance near the fluid. Predictable performance Designs characterised on our dedicated ejector test bench, including dilution rates. Proven designs About 2,500 steam jet ejectors delivered to La Hague (France), and others to Rokkasho Mura (Japan) and the Shaw/Areva MOX project (USA). Typical solution families Steam jet transfer ejectors Motive steam transfers or draws radioactive and chemical solutions between vessels. Versions with biological protection for highly corrosive and radioactive fluids. Ejectors for reactor safety Steam jet ejectors for reactor safety systems. Each ejector is sized for your fluid, flow and motive steam, drawing on data from our own test bench. Certifications & approvals ASME NQA-1 Company certification: ASME NQA-1 certified; 10 CFR 50, 10 CFR 71 and 10 CFR 21. ISO 9001:2015 Scope includes the design, manufacturing and sales of fluid transfer ejectors. Audited and/or approved vendor For applications in research centres, fuel production, fuel conversion, fuel enrichment, power plants, fuel transportation and used fuel reprocessing. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Ejector case studies are in preparation. Ask us for references in spent fuel reprocessing and research facilities. Share your application All case studies → Related literature Ask us for ejector technical data for your application. All literature → FAQ How does an ejector work? Motive steam accelerates through a nozzle and creates a low-pressure zone that draws in the fluid to be moved. The mixture then leaves through a diffuser. Is the transferred fluid diluted? Yes: the motive steam condenses into the fluid. We size each ejector to keep this dilution under control. All questions → Fluids & applications All fluids & applications Industries Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, flow rate, lift and available motive steam. Send an inquiry What next? Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations."}, {"u": "solution-instrumentation.html", "t": "Bellows sealed instrumentation valves, Model 2020 | Descote V2", "h": "Instrumentation valves", "d": "Model 2020 small-bore bellows sealed valves to isolate gauges, transmitters, flowmeters and sampling points on chlorine, HF, HCN and other hazardous lines.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Instrumentation Instrumentation valves Small-bore bellows sealed valves that isolate measuring and sampling points on hazardous fluid lines. Instrumentation descote has also successfully developed a full range of Model 2020 bellows-sealed globe valves for applications where zero ppm leakage to the atmosphere is a primary requirement. These valves are used in highly specific instrumentation applications in the chemical industry, handling halogens and their derivatives such as chlorine, A-HF, phosgene and other hazardous fluids. Their main application is as isolation valves on sample bottles, in laboratories, pilot units or analysis lines. Research centers Nuclear industry descote has also successfully developed a full range of bellows-sealed globe valves for highly specific applications involving heavy water, lead-lithium, and other specialized fluids in research centers. This equipment meets very high tightness standards. Pre-engineered or tailor-made A standard Model 2020 adapted to your instrument line, or a special small-bore valve designed with you. Pre-engineered solutions: manufacturing range → Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Zero leakage to the atmosphere Bellows sealing down to 1/8\", backed by secondary packing, where zero ppm leakage to the atmosphere is a primary requirement. Vacuum to high pressure Bellows sealing that stays tight from vacuum to high pressure; helium leak testing on request. Compact installations Forged body and a choice of end connections: butt-weld, socket-weld, threaded, compression tube fittings or flanges. Corrosive fluids Materials chosen for the process fluid, from stainless steel to nickel alloys such as Hastelloy® C-276. Typical solution families Model 2020 Manual bellows sealed instrumentation globe valve with a forged body. Standard range 1/8\" to 1/2\", Class 150 to 1500, −80 °C to +400 °C. Handwheel operation Straight or angle body Model 2020A The Model 2020 fitted with a pneumatic actuator for remote on-off duty. A control version is also available. Pneumatic actuator Solenoid valve and limit switches on request Even at half an inch, a descote valve is specified for your fluid, and its seat is gas-tested for zero leakage before delivery. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. PED 2014/68/EU Pressure Equipment Directive: made under our quality system approved to module H; the category depends on size and fluid. CRN Model 2020 included in our Canadian Registration Number (CRN) scope. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Instrumentation case studies are in preparation. Tell us about your application. Share your application All case studies → Related literature Instrumentation bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2020 Request All literature → FAQ Why a bellows sealed valve on an instrument line? A leak at a gauge or sampling point exposes operators as much as one on the main line. With a bellows, the packing is no longer the only barrier at the stem. Can the Model 2020 match our specification? Yes. Body material, end connections and pressure class are chosen for your line and fluid. Tell us your standard. All questions → Fluids & applications Also served Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, instrument type and connection standard. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions."}, {"u": "solution-model-1000.html", "t": "Model 1000 valve for UF6 cylinders | Descote V2", "h": "UF6 valve – Model 1000", "d": "The descote Model 1000: 1-inch valve for 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G UF6 cylinders, designed to ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195 and supplied to the nuclear fuel cycle since 1978.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Transport ▸ UF6 valve Transport · Nuclear UF6 valve – Model 1000 The 1-inch valve that closes the uranium hexafluoride (UF6) cylinders travelling between conversion, enrichment and fuel fabrication plants around the world. One valve, the whole fuel cycle Each UF6 cylinder has a single valve: the only way in and out for the product. The cylinder is filled through it at the conversion plant, emptied and refilled at the enrichment plant, then emptied again at the fuel plant. In between, it travels by road, rail and sea. The valve must stay tight for the whole journey: handling, transport, and heating for liquid-phase filling and emptying. We have supplied 1-inch cylinder valves to the fuel cycle since 1978, and are approved by the US Department of Energy (DOE). What the valve must withstand UF6 chemistry UF6 reacts with moisture to form hydrogen fluoride (HF): materials and stem sealing are chosen for fluorinated service. Heat and cold Designed for −40 °C to +121 °C, from winter transport to hot filling and emptying. One interface for every cylinder A tinned 1\"-11½ NGT tapered thread that fits any compliant cylinder. Traceability Each valve is identified and supplied with its material certificates, as ANSI N14.1 requires. UF6 valve at a glance UF6 valve – Model 1000 1-inch cylinder valve designed to ANSI N14.1 (Type 51 valve) and ISO 7195. 30B and 30C cylinders: enriched UF6 48X and 48Y cylinders: natural UF6 48G cylinders: depleted UF6 Standard by design, the Model 1000 is built under the same ISO 9001 and NQA-1 quality assurance as our process valves. Certifications & approvals The standards the Model 1000 is designed to, and the approvals behind it. Certificates on request. ANSI N14.1 US standard for UF6 packaging: cylinders, valves and plugs. ISO 7195 International standard for UF6 transport packagings, derived from ANSI N14.1. US Department of Energy descote is approved by the US DOE; our 1-inch cylinder valves were first found acceptable for its enrichment plants in 1979. Nuclear quality assurance Quality program to ASME NQA-1, 10 CFR 50 Appendix B, 10 CFR 71 and 10 CFR 21. All certifications & approvals → Related literature 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders Request Nuclear programme: descote in the nuclear industry Request All literature → FAQ Can a valve removed from a cylinder be reused? No. ISO 7195 requires new valves and plugs: each Model 1000 is delivered new, identified and certified. Do you also supply plugs and sampling valves? Yes: 1-inch plugs for UF6 cylinders, to ANSI N14.1, and ¾-inch valves for sampling bottles. Tell us your cylinder types and quantities. All questions → Fluids & applications Fluorine related Industries Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Transport Process / Piping Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your cylinder types, quantities and destination country. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Transport Valves for ISO containers and for the tank cars and trailers used to transport hazardous fluids. Industry Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Resources Literature Product brochures, maintenance manuals and safety instructions."}, {"u": "solution-process-piping.html", "t": "Process & piping valves for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Process / Piping valves", "d": "Bellows sealed 2100B and 2500 globe valves, 1500B gland packed, 3-way and 8000 check valves for chlorine, HF alkylation, HCN and other Category M services.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Process / Piping Process / Piping valves Manual, on-off and control globe valves for the most hazardous process fluids. Valve solutions for hazardous fluids The chemical and agrochemical processes based on chlorine, A-HF, phosgene… call for the highest level of tightness and safety. descote offers its valves for these process applications: bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B (bellows protected from the flow) and Model 2500 (bellows in the flow), available in manual, actuated or control versions, as well as lift check valves Model 8000. These valves are specifically designed for this field of application, with enhanced quality controls to ensure safety and reliability. Bellows sealed globe valves for critical service Nuclear industry In the general UF6 cycle, the processes are mainly based on the chemistry of fluorine, chlorine, and their derivatives. Our company offers its range of bellows sealed globe valves, Models 2100B and 4025, specifically designed for this field of application, with enhanced quality controls to ensure safety and reliability. High pressure globe valves Nuclear industry The development of the French electro-nuclear market has led us to develop a range of gland packed and bellows high-pressure valves for the primary and secondary circuits of nuclear reactors. The same equipment is also used for test reactor facilities as well as for ship and submarine propulsion systems. Pre-engineered or tailor-made A 2100B or 2500 adapted to your fluid, materials and standards, or a new design when no standard solution fits. Pre-engineered solutions: manufacturing range → Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Stem leakage A welded metal bellows seals the stem; secondary packing backs it up. Deposits A hard knife-edge seat cuts through deposits. Operation The plug presses onto the seat instead of sliding across it: the closing effort stays steady, even in an emergency. Typical solution families Also: the 2100HF series for HF alkylation, 1500B gland packed valves, 3100/3500 3-way valves, BIMATIC actuators. ← → 2100B Bellows protected from the flow, for liquefied gases, flashing and thermal shock. Standard range 1/2\" to 16\", −101 °C to +400 °C, up to Class 1500 (manual) or Class 600 (actuated). Manual 2100B On-off 2100BAT Control 2100BAC 2500 Bellows in the flow, for fluids that polymerise or crystallise. Same standard range as the 2100B. Manual 2500 On-off 2500BAT Control 2500BAC 8000 Spring-loaded lift check valve against reverse flow. Lift check Materials are chosen for your fluid and pressure class, then traced from raw material to final test. Certifications & approvals Certificates, approvals and declarations, on request. Euro Chlor 2100B, 2100BAT and 2100BAC Euro Chlor approved (GEST 17/492). Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6 Our full range of valves for chlorine service, liquid or gas, conforms to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. descote has been a member of the Chlorine Institute since 1985. HF alkylation Bellows sealed globe valves approved by UOP (a Honeywell company) for HF alkylation service. EN ISO 15848-1 Models 2100B, 2100BAT, 2500, 3100 and 3500 type-tested for fugitive emissions, class AH-CO3, and to VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). SIL 3 capable Series 1500, 2100, 2500, 4025 and 2200/2300, and our actuators, SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010. PED 2014/68/EU Pressure Equipment Directive, quality assurance module H. ATEX 2014/34/EU Equipment for explosive atmospheres: compliant with the directive; technical file lodged with a notified body. KHK (Japan) Our valves are approved by the High Pressure Gas Safety Institute of Japan (KHK). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Valve nest on top of a vessel, reached through the service grating. Europe · Liquid chlorine Chlorine feed line: 20 years without maintenance A 1-inch 2100B on a liquid chlorine feed line, maintenance-free in 2022. Process / Piping Chlorine related Chemicals Actuated bellows sealed globe valve on a process unit. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) HF alkylation in several refineries Isolation valves in HF alkylation units, praised for positive shut-off. Process / Piping Fluorine related Petrochemicals A row of manual globe valves with handwheels, ready for installation. Asia · Hydrogen cyanide (HCN) 550+ valves for one HCN unit More than 550 manual and on-off 2500-series valves, 1\" to 6\", up to Class 1500, in a single HCN unit. Process / Piping Cyanide related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2100B Request Bellows sealed globe valve, Model 2500 Request Lift check valve, Model 8000 Request HF alkylation: process valves Request All literature → FAQ Can a globe valve replace a gate, plug or ball valve? It can, at the same face-to-face (installed length). Globe valves pass less flow than full-bore valves, so we check your flow coefficient (Cv) first. All questions → Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Key fluid Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Key fluid Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Instrumentation Storage Transport Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Share your fluid and conditions. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Resources Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia."}, {"u": "solution-storage.html", "t": "Storage tank valves for liquefied toxic gases | Descote V2", "h": "Storage tank valves", "d": "Dual Tek top and bottom tank valves, Models 2200 and 2300: a bellows sealed angle valve with an internal safety check valve, for anhydrous HF, chlorine, ammonia and other liquefied gases.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Storage Storage tank valves Top and bottom tank valves that keep liquefied toxic gases contained, and close remotely when it matters. Storage The increased safety and reliability requirements of industries handling hazardous fluids have led descote to develop a solution dedicated to large-capacity tanks for storing dangerous liquefied gases such as A-HF, Cl2, NH3, and others. The Dual Tek system combines a bellows-sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve. These valves, Model 2200 and Model 2300, can be installed at the top or bottom of the tank. Pre-engineered or tailor-made A proven Dual Tek assembly adapted to your tank, or a new tank valve designed with you. Pre-engineered solutions: manufacturing range → Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Emergency isolation A spring-return actuator closes the valve, locally or by remote emergency command. Two barriers An internal safety check valve inside the tank, plus an external bellows sealed angle valve. Stem tightness Bellows sealing at the stem, backed by secondary packing. Typical solution families Dual Tek tank valves The Dual Tek system combines a bellows sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve, at the top or bottom of large tanks. Standard range 1\" to 8\", Class 150 to 600, remotely operated. 2200 – tank top, bellows protected from the flow 2300 – tank bottom, liquid outlet Your fluid, tank nozzle and shutdown logic set the design of each tank valve, built to the same quality plan as our process valves. Certifications & approvals Certificates on request. SIL 3 capable Models 2200 and 2300 are SIL 3 capable according to IEC 61508:2010, certified by exida as components. EN ISO 15848-1 Models 2200 and 2300 type-tested to EN ISO 15848-1 (fugitive emissions, class AH-CO3) and VDI 2440 (TA-Luft). All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Actuated globe valves in descote yellow on an outdoor process line. Europe · Liquid and gaseous chlorine 400 valves for a new chlorine storage unit Manual, on-off, control and tank-bottom valves, 1\" to 10\", for storage, liquefaction and sampling. Process / Piping Storage Chlorine related Chemicals Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Storage tank valves, Models 2200 & 2300 Request All literature → FAQ Is a SIL 3 capable valve enough for a SIL 3 loop? Not on its own. The SIL applies to the whole safety loop – valve, actuator, solenoid valve and logic – and must be demonstrated for each application. All questions → Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Process / Piping Transport Tailor-made Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, tank nozzle and safety requirements. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Transport Valves for ISO containers and for the tank cars and trailers used to transport hazardous fluids. Fluid & application Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene: PVC, isocyanates, chloromethanes and more. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up."}, {"u": "solution-tailor-made.html", "t": "Tailor-made valve engineering for hazardous fluids | Descote V2", "h": "Tailor-made engineering", "d": "Tailor-made valves for hazardous fluids: our skill set, valves built for one process, field cases. Engineered, made and tested in Feyzin, France.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Tailor-made Tailor-made engineering Whatever your specification, our teams can meet it, and develop a new product when no standard solution fits. Built on long experience in the chemical industry, descote brings recognized expertise to hazardous and critical fluid applications. The entire cycle is managed in-house: calculations, design, research, prototyping, testing, qualification and industrial production, together with project management, documentation and inspection. All of it is covered by our ISO 9001-certified Quality Assurance organization. Global project management and customer support are part of our DNA. Looking to develop a valve solution? Our R&D specialists, engineers and technical sales advisors will design a tailor-made solution with you and support you throughout your project. Engineering approach: our skill set A toolbox of skills and competences, all in-house: that is why we can engineer a valve for your specification, whatever it is. 01 Project management and customer support We support our customers throughout every stage of their projects, combining adaptability, rigor, international experience and a strong commitment to service. Project management Ability to adapt to different customer standards and quality requirements Support during customer audits Definition and monitoring of quality plans Coordination and follow-up throughout the project Customer support A strong focus on service and customer needs, in close collaboration with customers and partners Experience working across different cultures and working practices 02 International standards & compliance Valve standards (ATEX/PED, SIL, ASME, RCCM, AAR) and design codes (ASME B31.3, BS, API). 03 Fluid mechanics & engineering expertise Fluid mechanics and mechanical design: flow simulation, FEM calculation. 04 Materials & material manufacturing Metallurgy and materials: material processing, forged and cast construction. 05 Welding 06 NDT proficiency Non-destructive testing: radiography, magnetic particle and leak testing. Testing and qualification. 07 Tightness Sealing technology for zero-leakage performance. 08 Automation Control systems & I&C, process engineering, P&ID expertise. 09 Surface treatment & coating Corrosion protection: coatings and surface treatments. Built for one process Each valve shown here was built for one customer process: its medium, its pressure, its connections, its actuation. Large actuated valve, installed on site Special valve assembly Multi-port valve block Valve panel assembly UF6 Bellows sealed valve with star guided disc Chlorine gas Bellows sealed angle valve for pressure tapping Every design choice on this page traces back to your fluid, and every test result to your valve's serial number. Tailor-made in practice Top-mounted valves on a storage tank, painted descote yellow. North America · Anhydrous HF Anhydrous HF tank outlet Nickel-alloy bottom-outlet valves up to 8\": reliability study, helium testing, 18-metre manual extension. Storage Tailor-made Fluorine related Chemicals Large actuator on a valve assembly, with its control instrumentation. North America · Hydrogen fluoride (HF) Bespoke actuator, HF alkylation safety system A 10-inch 2100HF valve replaced plug valves, with a fail-open actuator designed by descote. Process / Piping Tailor-made Fluorine related Petrochemicals Pipe racks and valves of a process plant. Europe · Hydrogen Hydrogen at 420 bar A 1-inch Class 2500 gland packed valve for 420 bar, replacing a 2002 descote valve. Process / Piping Tailor-made Other critical applications Chemicals All case studies → Fluids & applications Also served Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Also served Cyanide related Hydrogen cyanide (HCN). Also served Other critical applications High-pressure hydrogen, bromine, ethylene oxide, molten salts, ammonia and other severe services. Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Agrochemicals Crop protection: herbicides, insecticides and fungicides. Petrochemicals Refineries, above all HF alkylation units. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Process / Piping Instrumentation Transport Storage Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Discuss your requirements Share your fluid, conditions and specification: our engineers will answer. Send an inquiry What next? Resources Case studies Anonymised field results in chlorine, hydrogen fluoride, hydrogen cyanide, nuclear and other severe services, in North America, Europe and Asia. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. descote Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France."}, {"u": "solution-transport.html", "t": "Tank car valves for liquefied toxic gases | Descote V2", "h": "Transport valves", "d": "AAR-approved bellows sealed tank car valves for chlorine, anhydrous HF and HCl, and Dual Tek valves for ISO tank containers.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions ▸ Transport Transport valves Valves that keep liquefied toxic gases contained on the move, by rail and road. Valves for ISO containers descote supplies valves for road and rail transport in ISO containers. These Dual Tek technology valves are specially designed to ensure the safety and reliability of transporting hazardous liquefied gases such as A-HF and Cl2. These products are ISO 10297 certified and comply with RID/ADR regulations. Road and rail transport valves descote offers a complete range of valves for tank cars and trailers used for transporting hazardous fluids. These bellows sealed valves, available in manual or actuated versions, can be fitted with an internal safety check valve. All models are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR). Valves for UF6 cylinders 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G Nuclear industry The storage and transport of UF6 (uranium hexafluoride) is mainly carried out in 30B, 48X, 48Y and 48G type containers. These containers are fitted with a 1″ isolation valve defined by ANSI N14.1 and ISO 7195 standards. descote is approved by the U.S. D.O.E. and has been supplying the global industry since 1978. descote also manufactures 1″ plugs for these containers, as well as ¾″ valves for sampling bottles. UF6 valve – Model 1000 → Pre-engineered or tailor-made Approved designs for rail, road and ISO containers; a new cargo or container starts a tailor-made project with you. Pre-engineered solutions: manufacturing range → Tailor-made engineering → Technical challenges addressed Containment after an accident Double closure: the tank stays closed even if the external valve is torn off. No operator on the tank Remote operation from the loading station, and automatic closure if the car moves during transfer. Stem tightness Bellows sealing, backed by an emergency stuffing box. Maintenance The main valve can be replaced without degassing the tank. Typical solution families ← → Road & rail transport valves Bellows sealed angle valves for tank cars and road tankers, manual or actuated, with an optional internal safety check valve. 921 manual valve 922/926 manual valve + internal check valve 925/926 pneumatic valve + internal check valve Valves for ISO containers Valves with our Dual Tek technology, also used on storage tanks, for road and rail transport of liquefied hazardous gases such as anhydrous HF and chlorine. UF6 valve – Model 1000 1-inch valve for UF6 cylinders. Explore the range → The 925/926 exists in separate approved versions for chlorine, anhydrous HF and anhydrous HCl: each valve is matched to its cargo, then traced by a unique serial number and certified material test reports. Certifications & approvals Approvals, and the standards our designs follow. Certificates on request. AAR Models 921 and 922 (manual) and 925 (pneumatic operated valve) are approved by the Association of American Railroads (AAR); our Feyzin plant is audited to AAR M-1003 quality requirements. Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 168 Our full range of valves for chlorine service, liquid or gas, conforms to Chlorine Institute Pamphlet 6. descote has been a member of the Chlorine Institute since 1985. Transport Canada 922/926 and 925/926 compliant with standard TP14877. ISO 10297 and RID/ADR ISO container valves certified to ISO 10297 and compliant with the RID (rail) and ADR (road) dangerous goods regulations. All certifications & approvals → Proven in the field Valves inside the protective housing of a rail tank car, seen from above. North America · Liquid chlorine Chlorine tank cars across North America Over 1,000 double-closure 922/926 valves: bellows sealed angle valve plus internal check valve. Transport Chlorine related Chemicals All case studies → Related literature Trailer & rail transportation valves Request All literature → FAQ What does double closure mean on a tank car? Two independent barriers: an internal spring-loaded ball check valve under the cover plate, and an external bellows sealed angle valve. How are valves prepared for chlorine service? They are degreased, dried and sealed before shipping. All questions → Fluids & applications Key fluid Chlorine related Chlorine, hydrogen chloride (HCl) and phosgene. Also served Fluorine related Hydrogen fluoride (HF) and fluorinated gases. Industries Chemicals Chlorine, fluorine and cyanide chemistry, from PVC and isocyanates to refrigerants. Nuclear Valves and ejectors across the fuel cycle, from conversion to reactors, reprocessing and research facilities. Other solutions Process / Piping Storage Tailor-made UF6 valve Discuss your requirements Send us your fluid, container type and applicable regulations. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Storage The Dual Tek system: a bellows sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve, at the top or bottom of large tanks. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. descote After sales Genuine spare parts, repair in Feyzin and repair shops close to your plants."}, {"u": "solutions.html", "t": "Valve solutions for hazardous applications | Descote V2", "h": "Valve solutions for hazardous applications", "d": "Bellows sealed valves and ejectors for chlorine, HF, HCN and other hazardous fluids: pre-engineered bases adapted to your fluid, or tailor-made engineering from scratch.", "x": "Home ▸ Solutions Valve solutions for hazardous applications Every descote valve starts from your fluid, your process and your standards. Choose a proven base or start from a blank page: either way, it is engineered for you. Valve solutions Two ways to the right valve: start from a field-proven design, or develop a new one with our engineers. Pre-engineered solutions Field-proven valve designs for highly hazardous fluids, adapted to your application, your materials and your standards. See the five categories → Tailor-made engineering When no standard solution fits: a new valve developed with you, from calculations to qualification, entirely in-house. See how we engineer it → Pre-engineered solutions descote offers a comprehensive range of valve solutions engineered specifically for highly hazardous fluids and critical environments. Pre-engineered does not mean off the shelf: we start from a field-proven design and adapt it to your needs. Precisely adapted to your applications and fluids, for safe and efficient operation Engineered to your requirements for materials, norms and international standards Built to withstand the toughest environmental constraints Face-to-face replacement of ball, plug and gate valves, with no pipe modification All descote valves are designed for dangerous, corrosive, inflammable, pyrophoric media, and particularly for all category M fluids as per ASME B31.3. descote bellows sealed globe valves for uncompromised safety and reliability The descote bellows sealed globe valve is Best Available Technology (BAT): it guarantees production efficiency and absolute safety by providing zero stem leakage and zero molecule emission, thanks to its multi-layer metal bellows welded to stem and bonnet. Reliable shut-off and control are ensured through pressing rather than sliding, which avoids friction and jamming over time. This unique design also features no dead volume, preventing any hazardous chemical buildup. Scale deposits are easily cut through by an innovative metal-to-metal knife-effect design. The descote bellows sealed globe valve eliminates fugitive emissions and protects against fluid hammer effects. Engineered with a heavy-duty construction and needle bearings, the valve ensures smooth, durable and tool-free operation, even in emergencies. descote valves are fire resistant by design, ensuring maximum safety in high-risk environments. Ball, plug & gate valve replacement descote offers a full range of valves that are fully interchangeable with ball, plug and gate valves, with no piping modifications required. Process / Piping Bellows sealed globe valves Model 2100B and Model 2500, manual, actuated or control, and lift check valves Model 8000. Discover → Instrumentation Model 2020 bellows sealed globe valves for zero ppm leakage: isolation valves on sample bottles, in laboratories, pilot units or analysis lines. Discover → Storage The Dual Tek system: a bellows sealed angle isolation valve with an internal safety check valve, at the top or bottom of large tanks. Discover → Transport Valves for ISO containers and for the tank cars and trailers used to transport hazardous fluids. Discover → Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors Steam jets for radioactive fluids: thermodynamic pumps without moving parts. Discover → Manufacturing range Valve technology Bellows sealed · Gland packed Replacements Gate valves · Ball valves · Plug valves Valve type Straight · Angle · 3-way change-over · Check valve Valve function Manual · On-off actuated · Control Materials CS · LTCS · SS · Monel · Inconel · Incoloy · Hastelloy · Nickel Dimensions DN15 (½″) to DN400 (16″), up to DN600 (24″) Rating ISO PN25 (150 lbs) to ISO PN250 (1500 lbs); from vacuum, up to ISO PN420 (2500 lbs) Temperature −101 °C (−150 °F) to 400 °C (750 °F); from −196 °C (−320 °F), up to 800 °C (1500 °F) Connections BW · Flanged · SW · Special Sealing type Simple · Welded lips · Leak detection · Secured leak detection Other construction & specific requirements Special designs, connections, packing, marking and painting Fluid transfer / Jet & Ejectors: ranges defined project by project. Materials At descote, material selection is never a standard choice: it is engineered for each application. Our valves are available in a wide range of materials, from carbon steels to high-performance alloys: Carbon steels Low-temperature carbon steels Stainless steels Special alloys: duplex, Hastelloy®, Inconel®, Incoloy®, Monel®, etc. Each material is chosen according to the actual service conditions (fluid, temperature, pressure) and the operating environment, including demanding locations such as tropical sites. Certificates and traceability With descote, every valve has a complete history. Our ISO 9001 quality system guarantees full traceability, from raw material to installation and throughout the valve’s service life: A unique identification number for each valve, ensuring lifetime traceability A Manufacturer Data Report documenting materials, tests, examinations and inspections Non-destructive testing and examination When handling hazardous and lethal fluids, there is no room for compromise. That is why descote applies some of the strictest inspection requirements in the industry, combining international standards (ASME, EN, MSS, ASTM), industry standards (Euro Chlor, Chlorine Institute), customer specifications and decades of field experience. Every valve undergoes systematic examinations: Radiography, ultrasonic, magnetic particle and liquid penetrant testing of welds and machined parts Wall thickness, dimensional, surface finish and hardness checks For the most critical applications, descote also offers additional in-house testing: positive material identification (PMI), helium leak and fugitive emission testing. Tailor-made engineering Whatever your specification, our teams can meet it, and develop a new product when no standard solution fits. The entire cycle is managed in-house: calculations, design, research, prototyping, testing, qualification and industrial production, together with project management, documentation and inspection. Engineering approach Our skill set: the in-house competences behind every tailor-made valve. Discover → Built for one process Examples of valves developed for a single application. Discover → Tailor-made in practice Field cases where descote developed the valve with the customer. Discover → Start from your fluid or your sector Fluids & applications → Industries → Every valve starts from your fluid and your process. Discuss your requirements Tell us about your fluid, operating conditions and standards. Our engineers will help you define the right valve. Send an inquiry What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Overview Fluids & applications Chlorine, fluorine, cyanide and other critical fluids. Overview Industries Chemicals, agrochemicals, petrochemicals and nuclear."}, {"u": "terms.html", "t": "Terms and Conditions | Descote V2", "h": "Terms and Conditions", "d": "Terms and conditions for using the descote website: access, intellectual property, technical information, liability and applicable law.", "x": "Home ▸ Terms and Conditions Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website. Legal text to be supplied by descote. The outline below lists the sections the final terms will cover. Terms of website use 1. Publisher and scope Identifies descote s.a.s. as publisher of the website and states who these terms apply to. Company details are given in our Legal notices. Legal notices → 2. Access to the website Availability of the website, maintenance, and our right to change, suspend or close it. 3. Intellectual property Protection of texts, photographs, drawings, videos, logos and descote trademarks, and the conditions for any reuse. 4. Technical information States that product information on this website is general and not contractual: each descote valve is defined for a specific application, and only descote's written proposal is binding. 5. Documents and literature Conditions for accessing and using brochures, manuals and other documents, including those available on request. Literature → 6. Inquiries and quotations States that sending a form does not place an order, and which terms govern descote offers and sales. 7. Liability Limits of liability for the use of the website and its content. 8. Links Links from this website to third-party websites, and links to this website. 9. Personal data and cookies How we handle personal data and cookies: see our Privacy Policy and Cookie Policy. Privacy Policy → 10. Changes to these terms How and when these terms may be updated, and the date of the current version. 11. Applicable law and jurisdiction Governing law and competent courts. 12. Contact descote s.a.s., 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès, 69320 Feyzin – France. info@descote.com Information on this site is general by design: every descote valve is defined, validated and tested for one specific application, and only a written descote proposal applies to it. A question about these terms? Please contact us through our inquiry form. Send an inquiry What next? Legal information Legal notices Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice."}, {"u": "globally.html", "t": "Our worldwide presence | Descote V2", "h": "Globally", "d": "Our worldwide presence ensures local support, faster delivery, and tailored solutions wherever you are.", "x": "Home ▸ descote ▸ Globally Globally 70+ countries served 9 repair shops 1 headquarters — Feyzin, France Need to contact us ? Need to get info ? All contacts Global presence Main Repair shops Countries shown on the map Repair shops Headquarters — Feyzin, France Global presence: countries shown on the map Argentina Australia Austria Bangladesh Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Croatia Czech Republic Denmark Ecuador Egypt Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Ireland Israel Italy Japan Jordan Kuwait Malaysia Mexico Morocco Netherlands New Caledonia New Zealand Norway Pakistan Peru Poland Portugal Qatar Romania Saudi Arabia Serbia Singapore Slovak Republic Slovenia South Africa South Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Tunisia Turkey United Arab Emirates United Kingdom USA Uzbekistan Venezuela Vietnam Repair shops Belgium Brazil China France Mexico Netherlands Taiwan United Kingdom USA Plus two local offices: Shanghai (China) and Baton Rouge (USA). Main — headquarters descote International 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès 69320 FEYZIN – FRANCE +33 4 72 89 25 00 Fax +33 4 72 89 25 25 info@descote.com Need a quotation or after-sales support? Our team answers every request from Feyzin. Send an inquiry Our subsidiaries descote Inc. – Baton Rouge, USA 11529 Sun Belt Court, Baton Rouge, Louisiana 70809 info.usa@descote.com Local stock of valves and actuators. descote Valve (Shanghai) Co., Ltd. – China 1126 Beisong Road, Minhang District, Shanghai 201111 Stock, customisation and after-sales for Asia-Pacific. Local contacts, one factory: wherever your plant is, your valve is designed and manufactured in Feyzin. Need a repair near your plant? Select “Repair shops” on the map above to find one close to your plant, or send us your request. Send an inquiry After sales What next? descote Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France. Resources Certifications & approvals Our certificates in force, from quality management to product approvals and national registrations. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solutions All solutions Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "inquiry.html", "t": "Inquiry | Descote V2", "h": "Contact", "d": "Get in touch with our experts for tailored guidance, pricing requests, or product insights—our know-how is at your service.", "x": "Home ▸ Inquiry Contact Request for quotation, after-sales service, maintenance or application study: tell us what you need. Name Company Email Industry (optional) — Chemicals Agrochemicals Petrochemicals Nuclear Other Your message I agree that my details are used to answer my request, as described in the Privacy Policy . Send my message Mock-up: nothing is sent. Thank you — your message has been noted. The descote team will get back to you shortly. descote 9 Avenue Jean Jaurès 69320 Feyzin – France +33 4 72 89 25 00 info@descote.com Worldwide Partners and repair shops close to your plants. Our network Every descote valve is defined for your fluid, your process and your standard. A few lines are enough to start: our engineers will ask for the rest. What next? Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. descote After sales Genuine spare parts, repair in Feyzin and repair shops close to your plants. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solutions Tailor-made All solutions"}, {"u": "join-us.html", "t": "Join us | Descote V2", "h": "Join us", "d": "Join descote in Feyzin, near Lyon, France: valve solutions for hazardous fluids. See our job openings or send an unsolicited application.", "x": "Home ▸ descote ▸ Join us Join us Chart a Course for Excellence - Join Us! Chart a Course for Excellence - Join Us! For over 50 years, our company, based in Feyzin (Lyon, France), has been designing and manufacturing valve solutions for hazardous fluids. On the demanding path of industrial progress, this family-owned business has stayed true to its founder’s original vision—with a lasting ambition: to protect people, drive sustainable innovation, and tackle the industry’s most critical challenges. Joining descote means stepping aboard for the long haul. Every team member is part of the crew—engaged in a shared mission where everyone plays a vital role. We pursue excellence and continuous improvement as our true north, helping us move forward together, no matter how rough the waters. Our playground? The entire world. Our edge? Advanced technology, powered by exceptional human chemistry. Looking for a company where your expertise is valued, innovation never stops, and every project has a purpose? Come aboard! descote in short A family-run company · Feyzin (Lyon, France) Valve solutions for hazardous fluids Chemicals · Agrochemicals · Petrochemicals · Nuclear Working at descote means building valves that are each defined for one customer's fluid, then machined, assembled and tested on our own benches in Feyzin. Career Opportunities CDI Technicien tourneur vertical traditionnel (H/F) See the offer None of the offers suit you? Use the form below to send us a speculative application and explain why you would like to join us. You have talent, we have challenges First name Last name Email Phone (optional) Type of request Unsolicited application Apply to an offer Offer (optional) — Technicien tourneur vertical traditionnel (H/F) Tell us about you Add my resume (optional) Add my cover letter (optional) I agree that my details are used to process my application, as described in the Privacy Policy . Send my application Mock-up: nothing is sent. Thank you — your application has been noted. We will come back to you soon. What next? descote Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France. descote Globally Representatives and repair shops close to your plants. Solution Tailor-made engineering No existing design fits? Our engineers specify a new valve with you, from the fluid up. Solutions Tailor-made Fluids & applications All fluids & applications"}, {"u": "legal-notices.html", "t": "Legal notices | Descote V2", "h": "Legal notices", "d": "Legal notices for the descote website: publisher, hosting, terms of website use, intellectual property and personal data.", "x": "Home ▸ Legal notices Legal notices Site provided by: DESCOTE 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière 69320 Feyzin – France Tél. : +33 (0)4 72 89 25 00 email : info@descote.com SIRET : 302 046 586 00046 RCS : 302 046 586 R.C.S. Lyon SAS with capital of € 1 659 300,00 Publishing Director: Vincent RICHER Contact : info@descote.com Web design and site development: Les Imageurs Hosting: Evoliatis 26 rue Bergson, 42000 Saint-Étienne Tél : 04 28 04 05 25 Terms of website use This page details the terms of use on which you may make use of any of the websites owned and managed by Us (\"our websites\"), whether as a guest or a registered user. Please read these terms of use carefully before you start to use a website. By using one of our websites, you indicate that you accept these terms of use and that you agree to abide by them. If you do not agree to these terms of use, please refrain from using any of our websites. Intellectual property The contents of this web site, text, images, sounds, animations, etc. as well as the graphic design and source code are protected by French and international law regarding the intellectual and industrial property rights of Steel Projects SAS. As such, their reproduction, distribution, public communication and transformation, totally or partially, is prohibited without the express authorization of Steel Projects SAS and constitutes an infringement sanctioned by articles L. 335-2 et seq. of the intellectual property code. Privacy Policy Steel Projects SAS informs that the personal data facilitated of voluntary form in this web site will be object of treatmen automated and incorporated to the corresponding files. The data incorporated to our files are absolutely confidential and will be dealed with the highest confidentiality and fulfilling all the requirements with Organic Law 13 of December 15/1999 on the Protection of Personal Data. The user will be able to use his right of access, rectification, cancellation and opposition of this data. Their personal data will not be yielded nor transferred to third. Cookies We may collect information about your computer, including where available your IP address, operating system and browser type, for system administration and to report aggregate information. This is statistical data about our users' browsing actions and patterns, and does not identify any individual. This information may be stored in a cookie on your computer or in a log file on our web server. A cookie is a small text file stored on the hard disk of your computer. Its contents are not transferred to or made available to any 3rd parties. We may also record statistics about which pages of our website you look at and include this information with any online form submissions you make. Our website uses cookies to identify registered users. Certain pages on our website are reserved for users who have completed and submitted a registration form. The cookie file does not contain your registration information but is used to verify your username and password when accessing certain pages and information on our website. You may refuse to accept cookies by adjusting the settings on your browser, however if you choose to do so you will not be able to access certain parts of our site. Our site changes regularly We aim to update our site regularly, and may change the content at any time. If the need arises, we may suspend access to our site, or close it indefinitely. Any of the material on our site may be out of date at any given time, and we are under no obligation to update such material. Les informations contenues dans ce site sont non contractuelles et sujettes à modification sans préavis. Web content and links Steel Projects SAS will not be held liable for the incorrect use which may occur to the contents on our web site, being the sole responsibility of the person that accesses or uses them. Nor do we assume any responsibility for the information contained on the web sites related to third parties which can be accessed by links or browsers from this web site. Events outside our control The service is normally accessible 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. We will not be liable or responsible for any failure to perform, or delay in performance of, any of our obligations under a Contract that is caused by events outside our reasonable control (\"Force Majeure Event\"). Our right to vary these terms and conditions We have the right to revise and amend any of our terms and conditions or policies from time to time. What next? Legal information Privacy Policy Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website."}, {"u": "privacy-policy.html", "t": "Privacy Policy | Descote V2", "h": "Privacy Policy", "d": "How descote uses the personal data sent through its contact forms, which browsing data it keeps, and how to correct or delete your data.", "x": "Home ▸ Privacy Policy Privacy Policy Personal information When you submit the contact form, DESCOTE may store: your surname, first name and e-mail address. Your consent is confirmed as soon as you submit the contact form. The form can only be validated if the box certifying your consent has been ticked. How do we use your data? DESCOTE uses your data to manage its customer/prospect relations. Their purpose is to facilitate the follow-up of assignments that have been entrusted to the centre and/or to send news and information that may be of interest to you. Browsing information (cookies) DESCOTE does not collect any personal data when you browse this site. Your IP address is completely anonymised and it is impossible to geolocate you. The only data we store is : the source of your visit (search engines, social networks, links, etc.) your use of the site (pages viewed, reading time, etc.) the hardware used (support, browser, screen size) We therefore consider that the cookies added to your computer are necessary for the site to function properly and for the site to be user-friendly during your visit. However, you can block the collection of cookies during your browsing. To do this, you need to change your browser settings. The settings for cookies are generally found in the \"Options\" or \"Preferences\" menu of your Internet browser. The following links will help you understand how to adjust these settings: Cookies used Our website uses cookies to ensure that certain parts of the website function correctly and that your preferences as a user are taken into account. These so-called \"functional\" cookies do not require your consent. Name of service provider Cookie name Shelf life Purpose DESCOTE _pk_id.nnnn 13 months Stores your unique visit identifier DESCOTE _pk_ref.nnnn 6 months Records the means by which you arrived on the site DESCOTE _pk_ses.nnnn 30 mins Allows temporary storage of your visit data DESCOTE hasConsent 7 months No longer displays the Cookies popup How do we use your data? DESCOTE uses your data to manage its customer/prospect relations. Their purpose is to facilitate the follow-up of assignments that have been entrusted to the centre and/or to send news and information that may be of interest to you. Your consent is given when you browse this site. Browsing information is used to provide you with an optimal browsing experience and to ensure the smooth operation of the services. Who has access to your data? DESCOTE staff may have internal access to your data. Subject to the user's contraindication, we may also be asked to pass on your data to our partners in order to carry out the tasks you have entrusted to us. These people may contact you directly using the contact details you have given us. They are not authorised to use your personal information other than for these purposes, and are required to keep it confidential. Where is your data stored? We use various security procedures to ensure the best possible protection for your personal data. Your personal data is stored in a secure, controlled computer area that is protected against unauthorised access. We also use the SSL encryption protocol on all pages of the https://www.descote.com website. The aim of these measures is to minimise the risk of unauthorised access to your data. However, there is no such thing as zero risk. How long will your data be kept? In order to respond as effectively as possible to the tasks entrusted to us, DESCOTE retains your data until the purpose for which it was collected has been fulfilled. Thereafter, your data will be deleted from our database. Navigation data (cookies) will be kept for 13 months, in accordance with regulations. Personal data will be kept for a maximum of 24 months, the retention period used to manage canvassing or commercial relations. You have the right to rectification, the right to be forgotten and the right to have your personal data deleted at any time. How can you access your data? If you identify an error in your personal data, or if you consider them to be incomplete or inappropriate, you may ask us to correct, complete or delete them. You can contact us by e-mail(info@descote.com), by telephone on +334 72 89 25 00, or by post at DESCOTE, 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière, 69320 Feyzin – France to ask us to take the necessary action. How can I unsubscribe from our communications? You can unsubscribe from our e-mails at any time by clicking on the \"Change your preferences\" or \"Unsubscribe from all lists\" links. You will find these links at the bottom of all our marketing and sales e-mails. You can also contact us by e-mail(info@descote.com), by telephone on +334 72 89 25 00 or by post at DESCOTE, 9 Av. Jean Jaurès Rue des Frères Lumière, 69320 Feyzin – France. We will continue to send you e-mails unless you change your mind or notify us otherwise. What next? Legal information Cookie Policy Which cookies this website uses, why, and how to change your choice. Legal information Terms and Conditions The terms that apply when you use the descote website. Legal information Legal notices"}, {"u": "index-egalite.html", "t": "Index égalité professionnelle femmes hommes | Descote V2", "h": "Index égalité professionnelle", "d": "Index de l'égalité professionnelle femmes-hommes de descote : résultats 2026 (données 2025) des indicateurs calculables.", "x": "Home ▸ Index égalité professionnelle Index égalité professionnelle Index égalité professionnelle femmes hommes La valeur de notre index 2026 basé sur les données 2025 n’a pas pu être calculé en raison de la nature de nos effectifs. Seuls deux indicateurs ont donné des résultats : Indicateur relatif à l’écart de rémunération : incalculable Indicateur relatif à l’écart de taux d’augmentation individuelles : 25 points / 35 Indicateur relatif au pourcentage de salariées ayant bénéficié d’une augmentation dans l’année suivant leur congé maternité : incalculable Indicateur relatif à la représentation parmi les plus hautes rémunérations : 5 point / 10 What next? descote Join us Join our teams in Feyzin, near Lyon, France. descote Company Our story since 1974, our values and our single factory in Feyzin, France. Legal information Legal notices"}];
